  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expanding the learning about Biosphere Reserves in Honduras through Rural Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this initiative, UNESCO and the Ministry of Education of Honduras, in collaboration with key stakeholders (i.e the MAB Committees) will provide opportunities to nearly 1000 rural indigenous K10-12 students attending 28 TVET agroforestry education centers in the dry corridor of Honduras to increasing their knowledge about Biosphere Reserves that are in the territories of their schools and communities, and learn how to use and live with them - concerning living with the nature, consumption and production models - with sustainability, involving also the application of ancestral knowledge.  Based on that knowledge, the initiative will also encourage students to develop skills for producing education materials that can be disseminated virtually throughout the country, to other rural education students, mainly those living in other Biosphere Reserves.</narrative>
  </description>
